  {
    "type": "patient_said",
    "state": "patient_speaking",
    "ts": 41.85889825,
    "turn": 1,
    "text": "Oh, well, that's not quite right, dear. My date of birth is August thirtieth, nineteen forty-six. Not July fourth. Let me just make sure you've got that correct before we go any further -- August thirtieth, nineteen forty-six. I want to make sure your records are straight, you know how it is.\n\nBut anyway, the reason I'm calling today is I need a refill on my celecoxib. That's the two hundred milligram tablets I take for my arthritis. My knees have been acting up something fierce, especially with all the bending down I do in that garden I was just telling you about. The weeding alone just kills me some days. I ran out about a week ago and I've been making do, but I really do need to get that prescription refilled if you can help me with that."
